      "evidence": {
        "source": "manual_review",
        "cve_id": null,
        "description": "Resembles SQL injection: the user-supplied query param q is interpolated into an f-string `like = f\"%{q}%\"` and passed into a DB filter, which taint-tracking scanners flag as string-built SQL. It is actually safe: the value is handed to SQLAlchemy ORM column expressions Ticket.subject.ilike(like) / Ticket.description.ilike(like) wrapped in or_(), so the user string is sent as a bound parameter, not concatenated into the SQL text. The f-string only adds LIKE wildcards around the already-parameterized value; no raw SQL or text() is constructed, and the base query is tenant-scoped via visible_ticket_query."
      },
      "false_positive_trap": true,
